{"created": "2019-12-03T20:28:00.016965+00:00", "modified": "2020-01-25T07:23:16.217999+00:00", "id": 3561115, "conceptrecid": "3561114", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3561115", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.3561114", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.3561115", "metadata": {"title": "JianyiCheng/HLS-benchmarks: HLS_Benchmarks_First_Release", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.3561115", "publication_date": "2019-12-03", "description": "<p>First release of my HLS benchmarks. The benchmarks include:</p>\n\n<ul>\n\t<li><em>gSum</em> sums a number of polynomial results from the array elements that meet the given conditions where the difference between two elements from the arrays is non-negative.</li>\n\t<li><em>gSumIf</em> is similar to <em>gSum</em> but the SS function returns one of two polynomial expressions based on the value of the difference.</li>\n\t<li><em>sparseMatrixPower</em> performs dot product of two matrices, which skips the operation when the weight is zero.</li>\n\t<li><em>histogram</em> sums various weight onto the corresponding features but also in a sparse form.</li>\n\t<li><em>getTanh</em> performs the approximated function <em>tanh(x)</em> onto an array of integers using the CORDIC algorithm and a polynomial function.</li>\n\t<li><em>getTanh(double)</em> is similar to <em>getTanh</em> but uses an array of doubles.</li>\n\t<li><em>BNNKernel</em> is a small BNN kernel with LUT function as XOR.</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jianyi Cheng", "affiliation": "Imperial College London"}], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/JianyiCheng/HLS-benchmarks/tree/v1.0", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "v1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "gpl-2.0-or-later"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "3561114"}}]}}, "title": "JianyiCheng/HLS-benchmarks: HLS_Benchmarks_First_Release", "links